How It Works
User: the user that logged in
Board: a workspace where lists belong (can have multiple)
Lists: Categories that categorise cards that belong to the board
Cards: Things the user has to do 


User Table - Stores information about everyone who signs up 

id: int
name: String
email: String (unique)
password: String
boards: Board[] - one user can own many boards ([] - means array)
createdAt DateTime @default(now())





Board Table - A board is an entire Trello workspace 

id: int
title: String
ownerId: int
owner: User @relation(fields: [ownerId], references: [id])
lists: List[] - every board has multiple lists


Information

gets the ownerId so that it knows which board belongs to which user e.g., board 5 belongs to user 1

owner User - allows access to while User object e.g., id, name, email, password, boards

owner User @relation(...) - tells Prisma these two models are connected (ownerID, and boardID)

fields: [ownerId] - answers which field in the board table stores the connection which is ownerId 
e.g., id: 1   
      title: University      
      ownerId: 3  
the ownerId is 3

references: [id] - answers which field in the User table does ownerId point to which is User.id
e.g., id: 1     name: Sarah
      id: 2     name: Mike
      id: 3     name: John

If ownerId is 3

ownerId -> User.id -> 3 -> John

so if there was no connection then the board would just know that the board belongs to userId 3 but not who they are 

the connection allows Prisma to know that the board belongs to userId 3 Prisma should know to look for userId 3 in the User table which allows Prisma to get the full user object for more information instead of just 3



